<title>BELGIUM: UM to up copper refining capacity further.</title>
<headline>UM to up copper refining capacity further.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1996-09-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Belgian non-ferrous metals group Union Miniere SA said on Tuesday its board had decided to add another 150,000 tonnes to a planned increase in copper refining capacity.</p>
<p>Together with the 200,000 tonnes already decided, capacity is now being increased by 350,000 tonnes a year.</p>
<p>The extra 150,000 tonnes capacity will cost 1.3 billion Belgian francs, the company said at the presentation of first-half results.</p>
<p>-- Brussels Newsroom +32 2 287 6810, Fax +32 2 230 7710</p>
</text>
